# Active-sampling instances

`samples.yaml` lists **20** kinetic instances, one per mechanism M1–M20.

Each entry:

| Field | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `mech_id` | `M1` … `M20` |
| `instance_id` | Label used in output folders |
| `k` | Rate constants for that mechanism (keys such as `k1`, `k2`, `k_-1`, …; `inhibitor` when the ODE has that species) |

The oracle integrates the matching entry in `config/mechanisms.yaml` with these `k` values. `[S]` / `[P]` are unitless (`S0 = 1`).
